    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 18th March 2004, the matter described above is lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nThe proposed extension, with dimensions 3.9m deep by 4.2m wide and with a height of 2.95m, that adds 48.44m3 to the volume of the original dwellinghouse, shown on the plans reference no. ASB/01 received by Council on the 9th March 2004 constitutes permitted development as defined by Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (as amended) and therefore does not require planning permission.\r\n"
